=== MODES ===
accessMode values (use exactly these strings):
  READ-ONLY  = only reads the Resource
  WRITE-ONLY = only modifies the Resource
  READ-WRITE = reads and modifies the Resource
  NO-ACCESS  = does not interact with the Resource
  DYNAMIC    = creates or destroys the Resource at runtime

concurrency = integer >= 1 (max number of parallel tests that may use this Resource).
sharing     = true or false (true if the Resource instance may be shared between concurrent tests).


=== TASK ===

{#- Be Clear and Precise and CoT -#}
Work through these steps in order. Think step by step before answering.


1. Parse the test method. List every method call reachable from the test prefix and the test body.
2. For each call, decide whether it transitively touches a Resource in the Resource list. Note the test step method that performs the access.
3. Classify the interaction as READ-ONLY, WRITE-ONLY, READ-WRITE, NO-ACCESS, or DYNAMIC, and assign the concurrency and sharing values, based on what the step method does to the Resource.
4. If the test appears to need a Resource that is NOT in the Resource list, do NOT invent an annotation for it. Record it in the Suggested Resources section at the end.
{#- Re-reading -#}
5. Self-check: re-read the test once more. Confirm every annotation is supported by a specific line of code. Drop any annotation you cannot justify.

Rules:
- Only annotate Resources that appear in the Resource list.
- If a Resource has conflicting interactions in the same test, collapse them into READ-WRITE.
- Every test must produce at least one annotation.
- Use the exact resID strings from the Resource list (case-sensitive, no quoting changes).

=== OUTPUT ===
Produce three parts in this exact order. Use these exact section labels, in plain text, with no extra commentary before or after them.

Part 1 - Explainability:
One bullet per annotated Resource, in the same order as the Java block below. Format each bullet as:
- <resID> via <stepMethod>: <one-sentence reason for the chosen access mode>

Part 2 - Annotations:
A single fenced Java code block. Inside the fence, output only @AccessMode lines, one per annotated Resource, in the same order as the bullets above. No comments, no other Java syntax.
```java
@AccessMode(resID="<resource>", concurrency=<N>, sharing=<true|false>, accessMode="<READ-ONLY|WRITE-ONLY|READ-WRITE|NO-ACCESS|DYNAMIC>")
```

Part 3 - Suggested Resources:
Resources the test seems to require but are absent from the Resource list. Format each bullet as `- <name>: <one-sentence reason>`. If every required Resource is already in the Resource list, write exactly `(none)` on a single line.
